      "content": "<h3>Stack as the modern Deque</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Signature:</strong> <code>Deque<E> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();  push, pop, peek</code></li>\n<li><strong>Returns:</strong> LIFO with a clean API</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> O(1)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For freshers:</strong> The recommended replacement is <code>ArrayDeque</code> used through the <code>Deque</code> interface. It has the same <code>push</code>, <code>pop</code> and <code>peek</code> names but offers only end operations, is not synchronized (so faster) and returns <code>null</code> from <code>peek()</code> on an empty stack.</p>\n<p><strong>For experienced developers:</strong> Differences to remember: <code>Deque.pop()</code> throws <code>NoSuchElementException</code> (not <code>EmptyStackException</code>), <code>peek()</code> returns <code>null</code>, <code>ArrayDeque</code> forbids <code>null</code> elements, and iteration goes from the <strong>top</strong> down.</p>",
